List inference backends.

Fields:
  NAME      canonical, version-explicit model name; aliases are also accepted
  BAND      normalized capability peg: L1 basic, L4 steerable minimum, L5 frontier; '-' is
            unpegged and '~' means not measured. Agents inherit this band
  KIND      authentication path: subscription, api, or local; not billing mode
  PROVIDER  backend/provider family used for authentication and routing
  TARGET    default provider-side id passed to a tool; a tool-specific id may
            override it, which `agents show NAME` displays
  ALIASES   alternate accepted names, including a derived family alias
  RING      source of the selected definition (explained below)

Bands are comparable across providers; vendor tier names are not mapped
positionally. For pegged rows JSON reports the numeric band and band_source
(declared, operator, measured, or cascade); unpegged rows omit both.
JSON source is the model's cloud/local inference path, not its RING.

RING is the source of this selected definition, not where an executable or
model runs: embedded = compiled baseline (the tool launch contracts plus the
seeded model/agent roster; BASHY_FLEET_SEEDS=off drops the roster, never the
contracts); shared = read-only directory from BASHY_TOOLS_PATH,
BASHY_MODELS_PATH, or BASHY_AGENTS_PATH; cloud = organization catalog cached by
sync; local = writable host override under BASHY_FLEET_DIR or the noun-specific
BASHY_*_DIR. Precedence is embedded -> shared -> cloud -> local. A local file
with overlay: true merges its present fields onto the next lower entry;
an older full file remains a complete replacement until migrated.

By default, list shows selected definitions from the embedded, shared, and
cloud rings and hides local custom definitions. --custom shows only local;
--all shows every ring; --ring all|embedded|shared|cloud|local selects a precise
ring. These flags are alternatives. A local override of a seeded name has
RING local because local supplied the selected definition. Text and JSON use
the same view; only text prints a hint when custom definitions are hidden.

Usage:
  model [flags]
  model [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add an inference backend to the local store
  budget      Inspect configured budgets and outstanding reservations
  edit        Open an entry in $EDITOR
  help        Help about any command
  limits      Inspect known account limits, resets and unavailable sources
  list        List inference backends
  migrate     Review and migrate a full-copy local override to a sparse overlay
  rm          Remove an entry from the local store
  schema      List fields accepted by --set, --unset, and --field
  set         Modify an inference backend
  show        Print a model's definition
  sync        Pull the org catalog into the overlay ring
  usage       Observe model usage and spend across shared accounts
  verify      Check that an entry is usable on this host

Flags:
      --all            show every ring, including otherwise hidden entries
      --band int       only models in exactly this band (1-5)
      --custom         show only local custom definitions
  -h, --help           help for model
      --json           emit JSON
      --min-band int   only models in this band or above (1-5)
      --ring string    show exactly one ring: all, embedded, shared, cloud, or local

Use "model [command] --help" for more information about a command.
